<h1>Motorcycle Trip to Moscow Idaho to ride the mountains of Idaho. May 11, 2021 Thru May 14, 2021.</h1>
<br>
<a href="https://www.google.com/maps/d/viewer?mid=1bfNw9dhBapnPAoCuTMLI77RCjMZREYSK" target="_blank"><IMG SRC="Motorcycle/motorcycle_moscow_20210511-20210514.jpg"  ALIGN=RIGHT style="width:700;"></A>
A map of the route to Moscow, Idaho. Ultimately this was just to ride across the WA State 20 'North Cascades" pass and then to the back roads of Idaho. The North Cascades pass hod *just* opened 5 days earlier. You can see the snow and video on the first day trip description. The entire ride was clear and beautiful, a perfect temperature (a little cold in the morning, but nice and warm later in the day).
<br><br>
The trip was a good mental break between a job change and COVID-19 'pandemic' stresses (yes, I was fully vaccinated before the trip). I was asked 'so, where are you going to go ...' I replied 'Elk City, Idaho ... Not sure what is in Elk City but the road going to there is Idaho State route 14. A road of 40+ miles that follows EVERY curve of the river'. Sometimes it is the ride that gets you there, not the destination.
<p style="clear:both;"></p>
<br><br>

<h3>The four-day trip</h3>

<ul type=disc>
 <li><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/d/viewer?mid=14T8u24PK5Tef4ksE4R3LP9PYVCfZ4REE" target="_blank"><IMG SRC="Motorcycle/motorcycle_moscow_20210511.jpg" ALIGN=RIGHT style="width:592px"></A>Trip Day One May 11, 2021: Ride north headed for Winthrop, WA, nice easy quick 170 mile ride. The ride was amazing all day long - <a href="motorcycle_moscowid_2021-05-11.html">Click for details of Day 1 of the ride</a> ...<p style="clear:both;"></p><BR>
	</li>
 <li><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/d/u/0/viewer?mid=1-xMT4Nkm3BgPM2K5Ik4_-ZP5kLA_Z5lL" target="_blank"><IMG SRC="Motorcycle/motorcycle_moscow_20210512.jpg" ALIGN=RIGHT style="width:592px"></A>Trip Day Two May 12, 2021: Ride from Winthrop, WA, to Moscow Idaho about 255 miles. Riding out of the mountains and across the plains of Eastern Washington - <a href="motorcycle_moscowid_2021-05-12.html">Click for details of Day 2 of the ride</a> ...<p style="clear:both;"></p><BR>
	</li>
 <li><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/d/viewer?mid=1j0hkklh5iRR2ky1TJ7WIs03VFewkg0zp" target="_blank"><IMG SRC="Motorcycle/motorcycle_moscow_20210513.jpg" ALIGN=RIGHT style="width:592px"></A>Trip Day Three May 13, 2021: LONG day in the saddle, almost 12 hours and 400+ miles, but I had a smile on my face at the end - <a href="motorcycle_moscowid_2021-05-13.html">Click for details of Day 3 of the ride</a> ...<p style="clear:both;"></p><BR>
	</li>
 <li><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/d/u/0/viewer?mid=10yCQ5r2L3gzBaokQ6UHat6E4Na2KdvJJ" target="_blank"><IMG SRC="Motorcycle/motorcycle_moscow_20210514.jpg" ALIGN=RIGHT style="width:592px"></A>Trip Day Four May 14, 2021: Ride from Moscow Idaho back. Nice easy 250+ mile ride. The ride was sunshine and great weather all day long (as always coming across the pass with some wind, you see windmills for a reason) - <a href="motorcycle_moscowid_2021-05-14.html">Click for details of Day 4 of the ride</a> ...<p style="clear:both;"></p><BR>
	</li>
</ul>

